# Windsurf Cascade Rules: UI Pipeline

When the user asks to build, modify, or design UI components, websites, or frontend interfaces, activate the 6-stage UI Pipeline:

1. BRIEF INFERENCE:
   - Output: "Reading this as: <page kind> for <audience>, with <vibe> language, leaning toward <aesthetic>."
   - Declare values for DESIGN_VARIANCE (1-10), MOTION_INTENSITY (1-10), VISUAL_DENSITY (1-10).

2. DESIGN TOKENS & ANTI-SLOP:
   - Single accent color (< 80% saturation). Banish generic AI purple glows and warm cream/clay tropes.
   - Enforce uniform corner radius: lock to rounded-none, rounded-xl, or rounded-full.
   - Use clean modern sans (Geist, Outfit, Satoshi). Restrict body to max 65ch.
   - Maintain WCAG AA contrast (>= 4.5:1).

3. ASSET STRATEGY:
   - Domain-grounded 3D only. Pause offscreen with IntersectionObserver. Static fallback on prefers-reduced-motion.
   - No fake mockup divs. Real SVGs from Simple Icons.

4. LAYOUT & HERO ARCHITECTURE:
   - Hero min-h-[100dvh], top padding <= pt-24.
   - Strict 4-element hero budget (eyebrow, headline <=2 lines, subtext <=20 words, max 2 CTAs).
   - Asymmetric split layout when variance > 4.
   - Desktop nav single line (height <= 72px).
   - Multi-column grids must collapse to grid-cols-1 on mobile (< 768px).

5. MICRO-PHYSICS:
   - Animate ONLY transform and opacity.
   - Never use useState in scroll or pointer listeners.
   - Tactile feedback: active:scale-[0.98].

6. PRE-FLIGHT AUDIT:
   - Ban all em-dashes (— and –).
   - Verify all 9 checklist points prior to output.
